{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":630022,"ns":0,"title":"Abstract nonsense","extract":"In mathematics, abstract nonsense, general abstract nonsense, generalized abstract nonsense, and general nonsense are nonderogatory terms used by mathematicians to describe long, theoretical parts of a proof they skip over when readers are expected to be familiar with them. These terms are mainly used for abstract methods related to category theory and homological algebra.","description":"Tongue-in-cheek description of category theory and abstract mathematics","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}